      make scan ARGS="-e scan_oscap_force=true"
{% endif %}

WHAT THIS MEANS
  Nothing in this estate updates itself. That is a deliberate trade recorded in
  docs/unattended.md — packages install on demand and images are digest-pinned,
  so that nothing shifts underneath while nobody is watching. The cost of that
  trade is the number at the top of this report, and the reason this scan
  exists is that the number was previously unknown rather than accepted.

  Acting on it is a manual decision, not something this job will ever take.
  Applying errata is dnf's security-only upgrade path, run on the host by hand
  and followed by the reboot a kernel or glibc advisory will usually require.
  The exact command is deliberately not quoted here: tests/validate_scan_readonly.py
  fails the build if an upgrade invocation appears anywhere under a scan path,
  and that gate should not have to tell prose apart from a task.
